        <mxCell id="cap" value="Figure 1. Score-based generative modelling through SDEs, drawn from the repository at commit cb1f359. (a) A forward SDE takes data x(0) to noise; the three families in sde_lib.py differ only in f and g, and d(t) = 1 - exp(-2 B(t)) is the sub-VP discount. The network is trained by denoising score matching on the perturbed sample, in the configuration used here without likelihood weighting. (b) Reversing the same SDE in time generates samples: one corrector step then one predictor step per timestep, repeated N = 1000 times. The probability flow ODE is the deterministic alternative; run from the prior it produces samples, and run forwards from a data point it produces that point's latent code and an unbiased estimate of its log-likelihood. (c) The score network for the ve/cifar10_ncsnpp_continuous configuration. Block width and height are the spatial resolution, which is also written inside each block; the bold line below each block is the channel count and the number of BigGAN residual blocks at that resolution, four per encoder level and five per decoder level. Attention is applied at 16² and once in the 4² bottleneck. The time embedding is added inside every residual block; the single green arrow stands for that shared conditioning. Not drawn: FIR up and downsampling, skip rescaling and the residual input pyramid (progressive_input = residual), all of which are configuration flags rather than separate stages." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Times New Roman;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#3C4350;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="966" width="940" height="140" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
